# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EN3150 A03 - what stays out of the repository
#
# Rule of thumb: anything that can be REGENERATED from code + config is
# ignored, EXCEPT results/metrics, results/figures and results/tables - and
# the notebooks, which are committed WITH their outputs.
# Those are committed on purpose - Member 4 cannot build the Section 6
# comparison table without every other member's metrics JSON, and nobody
# should have to re-run 20 epochs of training just to redraw a table.
# See CONTRIBUTING.md -> "What is and is not committed".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Virtual environments ---------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Local settings and secrets ---------------------------------------------
# A .env may hold personal values or a token, and the repository is public.
# .env.example is the committed template - see its header.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Tooling caches ---------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Datasets (large, downloadable, reproducible from configs/stages/data.yaml)
data/raw/**
data/processed/**
!data/raw/README.md
!data/processed/README.md

# The split definition IS committed - it is the reproducibility contract.
!data/splits/
!data/splits/*.csv
!data/splits/*.json
!data/splits/README.md

# --- Model weights (too large for git; regenerate by re-running the notebook) -
# Includes artifacts/checkpoints/_debug/, where synthetic and debug runs save.
artifacts/checkpoints/**
artifacts/exports/**
!artifacts/checkpoints/README.md
!artifacts/exports/README.md
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.tflite
!tests/fixtures/**/*.pt

# --- Synthetic fixture (generated on demand by MODE = "synthetic") -----------
# Deterministic, so regenerating it is cheaper than committing it.
tests/fixtures/synthetic/

# --- Editors / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Report build leftovers -------------------------------------------------
report/*.aux
report/*.log
report/*.out
report/*.synctex.gz
MEMBER_3_GUIDE.md

# --- Local workflow notes ---------------------------------------------------
/MEMBER_4_WORKFLOW.md
/MEMBER_4_IMPLEMENTATION_GUIDE.md
